  "implemented": [
    "Public retained arguments are only task and UUID attachment IDs; no filename, path, receipt, document or root permission is accepted. Native stamps a distinct private lease; direct public Source invocation refuses.",
    "Actual bounded scalar task/group/former/anchor/project/agent read scopes and saved metadata remain immutable and current through all phases. Active task agents continue under application ownership; opening has no mutation-only grants or legacy full-row/credential getters.",
    "TaskAttachmentFileOwner derives the literal saved namespace, supports metadata-only opening up to 64MiB, and retains an actual no-follow/nonblocking single-link regular-file FD through raw native acknowledgement. Root/task/file size/identity/mtime/ctime checks run before and after; no contents are read or transferred.",
    "Private nine-field receipts constrain exact UUID/name/task/root/target and finite u64 identities. Native validates these observations against its separately captured attachment-root descriptors using the existing unchanged workspace FD authority after strict transformation.",
    "Actual Linux pinned opener is guarded by the expected native physical main window, document receipt, trusted origin and current engine epoch before and after launch. Missing capabilities/hosts and retired documents refuse before effects.",
    "Callback and FD work remains owned through raw completion despite dropped public waiters or cancellation. Native roots close after callback drainage; uncertain exact Source FD closure blocks profile release and new file effects until explicit retry.",
    "Production namespace deletion is fenced during pending attachment file work. Open never alters metadata or file bytes and does not automatically replay accepted/uncertain OS effects."
  ],
